            "elements": [
                {
                    "type": "header",
                    "content": "Overview",
                    "level": 2
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "A project I worked on over the summer was learning how to build a robot arm. I entered the project not really knowing much and never really doing anything at this sort of level. To really get the full experience, I designed the whole arm in Fusion360, printed the parts on a Bambu Lab A1, designed the control circuit in KiCad, soldered the electronics onto perfboards, and programmed the controls in C++.",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 10
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "header",
                    "content": "Contents",
                    "size": 2,
                    "level": 3,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 15
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "The project has been broken into these main sections:",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 5
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                        "_|The CAD|(#cad)_",
                        "_|The Build|(#build)_",
                        "_|The Electronics|(#electronics)_",
                        "_|The Programming|(#programming)_",
                        "_|The Results|(#results)_"
                    ],
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 5
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "If there's any other info you need (items ordered, CAD files, tools used, etc.), do not hesitate to reach out. [@joshtreid08@gmail.com](mailto:joshtreid08@gmail.com)"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section",
            "positioning": {
                "marginTop": 20
            },
            "elements": [
                {
                    "type": "header",
                    "content": "The CAD",
                    "id": "cad",
                    "level": 2
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "All of the CAD was done in Fusion360. Having never really done this before, this was a huge learning process. Many hours were spent starting at a blank screen, unsure of where to even start. I watched [builds of other designs](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D1tMTEYRVEs&list=PLSueoDrBt5MMTL9O8qAWZiJrNIf8-29Qz&index=4) step-by-step to get as much of an idea as possible, but I wanted to avoid using any pre-made CAD designs."
                },
                {
                    "type": "header",
                    "content": "Base",
                    "level": 3,
                    "size": 2,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 20
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "The first part designed was the base. It consists mainly of a large 120T pulley driven by a 20T pulley on a stepper motor. A ball bearing is pressed against the belt to apply tension. Down the center of the base is a hole to run wires through. It is covered by a cap in the screenshot, but that's not part of the final design.",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 5
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "image",
                    "url": "/images/robot-arm/base.webp",
                    "alt": "Fusion screenshot of robot arm base.",
                    "title": "Robot Arm-Fusion-Base",
                    "screenSizes": {
                        "small": 100,
                        "medium": 80,
                        "large": 90
                    },
                    "width": 100,
                    "y": 50,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 10
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "note",
                    "level": "normal",
                    "content": "All of the stepper motors are NEMA-17 Stepper Motors",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 10
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "header",
                    "content": "Shoulder",
                    "level": 3,
                    "size": 2,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 20
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "The next part is the shoulder joint. The shoulder joint consists of a 20T driving a 100T pulley. The 100T pulley sits on a shaft with another 20T pulley, which drives another 100T pulley, giving an overall 25:1 gear ratio. To tension the belts, the stepper can move horizontally, and the other belt is tensioned by a small ball bearing.",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 5
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "image",
                    "url": "/images/robot-arm/shoulder.webp",
                    "alt": "Fusion screenshot of robot arm shoulder.",
                    "title": "Robot Arm-Fusion-Shoulder",
                    "screenSizes": {
                        "small": 100,
                        "medium": 80,
                        "large": 90
                    },
                    "y": 20,
                    "width": 100,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 10
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "header",
                    "content": "Arm Links",
                    "level": 3,
                    "size": 2,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 20
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "Both of the arm links are fairly straightforward designs. Two servos sit on the lower arm link (1st link) and the wrist (3rd link), and connect to the middle second link. The lower servo has 270deg range, and the upper servo has 180deg range.",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 5
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "image",
                    "url": "/images/robot-arm/arm.webp",
                    "alt": "Fusion screenshot of the robot arm links.",
                    "title": "Robot Arm-Fusion-ArmLinks",
                    "screenSizes": {
                        "small": 100,
                        "medium": 80,
                        "large": 90
                    },
                    "y": 40,
                    "width": 100,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 10
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "note",
                    "level": "normal",
                    "content": "All of the servos are DS3225 Servos",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 10
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "header",
                    "content": "Claw",
                    "level": 3,
                    "size": 2,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 20
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "The claw design uses a four-bar linkage design. The two large gears rotate together by a servo underneath. It's a little grayed out in the screenshot, but the claw sits on a servo on the wrist, allowing it to roll.",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 5
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "image",
                    "url": "/images/robot-arm/claw.webp",
                    "alt": "Fusion screenshot of robot arm claw.",
                    "title": "Robot Arm-Fusion-Claw",
                    "screenSizes": {
                        "small": 100,
                        "medium": 80,
                        "large": 90
                    },
                    "y": 40,
                    "width": 100,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 10
                    }
                }
                
            ]
        },
        {
