                    "content": "Assembling",
                    "level": 3,
                    "size": 2,
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 20
                    }
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "Parts were either screwed into inserts or had a nut on the other side. Most parts used M3 screws or M2 for the tiny parts. The timing belts had to be cut to the right [length](https://www.technobotsonline.com/gt2-pulley-belt-length-calculator.html) and the ends glued together to form a closed loop.",
                    "positioning": {
                        "marginTop": 5
                    }
                },
